## 1. ACTIONABLE REQUIREMENTS

| # | Requirement | Details & Implementation |
|---|-------------|--------------------------|
| 1 | **Define the survey scope** | <ul><li>Choose one region at a time (comment on issue #11 indicating which region is being tackled).</li><li>Break each region into a list of candidate agencies (per the issue description and local knowledge).</li><li>Record for each agency: <ul><li>Country & organization name</li><li>Data types (discharge, level, rainfall, groundwater, etc.)</li><li>Portal URL & map viewport (for devtools)</li><li>Whether an API endpoint exists (browser devtools or direct URL)</li><li>Registration/key requirements</li><li>License & redistribution terms (link to the exact document)</li></ul></li></ul> |
| 2 | **Validate each candidate** | <ul><li>Open the agency’s data portal in a browser (or using headless tools) and inspect network traffic on any interactive map.</li><li>Identify JSON/CSV/WFS endpoints that serve the relevant variable (e.g., `/api/v2/hydrometrie/stations/{stationId}/readings`).</li><li>Test a single call with `curl` (or an equivalent HTTP client) and capture a working example (raw request URL, headers, sample response). Record a minimal reproducible command.</li><li>If the endpoint requires a key, follow the signup flow and note the key URL.</li><li>If the portal is behind a login or the API times out, mark as “unreachable”.</li></ul> |
| 3 | **Populate the documentation table** | <ul><li>Add one row per surveyed agency to `docs/data_sources.md` (append after the existing “Sources” table).</li><li>Use the same column set as the existing rows: <code>Source</code>, <code>Region</code>, <code>Data Types</code>, <code>API</code>, <code>Status</code>.</li><li>Fill with the collected data; use “–” or “None found” where information is unavailable.</li><li>Include a **working example call** column (e.g., a `curl` snippet) for reachable sources.</li></ul> |
| 4 | **Record licensing & redistribution** | <ul><li>Copy the exact licence text (or a link) into the new `API Keys — what you need before collecting` section if a key is required.</li><li>Set `redistributable: true` only when the licence explicitly permits mirroring; otherwise leave it false.</li></ul> |
